Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:21:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Read legacy member fields: ordinal reference fields and
 unsigned integers

Integer-reference fields (0x0304) whose values are member ordinals rather
than note records, such as _Sort in the 2011 NHS semi-custom profiles,
are exported as int64 instead of failing the dimension, and unsigned
integer fields (0x0002, such as _Decimals) are read like signed ones.
Before this, to_arrow() raised "referenced member text is not a byte
vector" on these tables and both dimensions had empty metadata labels.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
