+### Fixed
+
+- Legacy member fields no longer fail a dimension: integer-reference fields (`0x0304`) whose values are member ordinals rather than note records, such as `_Sort` in 2011 NHS semi-custom profiles, are exported as `int64`, and unsigned integer fields (`0x0002`, such as `_Decimals`) are read like signed ones. Previously `to_arrow()` raised `referenced member text is not a byte vector` and the metadata labels of both dimensions were silently empty.
+
